  "title": "Watson and Crick publish the double-helix structure of DNA",
  "summary": "James Watson and Francis Crick, who worked at the Cavendish Laboratory in Cambridge, proposed the double-helix structure of DNA in a one-page paper in Nature on 25 April 1953. Their model paired the bases A with T and C with G inside two backbones, which suggested a mechanism for copying genetic material.",
